  "year": 2025,
  "arxivId": "2505.18536",
  "abstract": "This position paper argues that reinforcement fine-tuning (RFT) can significantly enhance the reasoning capabilities of multimodal large language models (MLLMs). RFT has been successfully applied to various MLLMs, demonstrating its potential in improving reasoning abilities across diverse modalities, tasks, and domains. The paper provides a comprehensive overview of the current state of RFT in MLLMs, including its background, successes, and future directions.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "The Core Idea",
      "content": "Reinforcement fine-tuning (RFT) is a technique that enhances the reasoning capabilities of large language models (LLMs) and multimodal large language models (MLLMs). <strong>RFT works by fine-tuning a pre-trained model using reinforcement learning</strong>, which involves training the model to maximize a reward signal. This technique has shown significant potential in improving the reasoning abilities of LLMs and MLLMs, making them more proficient across diverse modalities, tasks, and domains.",
