    {
      "title": "How It Works",
      "content": "RFT involves fine-tuning a pre-trained model using reinforcement learning. The process typically consists of three stages: <strong>pre-training</strong>, <strong>fine-tuning</strong>, and <strong>evaluation</strong>. During pre-training, the model is trained on a large dataset to learn general language understanding. In the fine-tuning stage, the model is fine-tuned using reinforcement learning to optimize its performance on a specific task. Finally, the model is evaluated on a test dataset to measure its performance.",
